# Extra instructions Cloudflare sends to the browser with each file (QA defects D-03 and D-16).
# Cloudflare already adds HSTS and "nosniff" from the dashboard (SSL/TLS, Edge Certificates).
# Content-Security-Policy is left out on purpose: add it later in report-only mode, because the
# site loads GSAP, YouTube, Formspree and the editor's scripts (unpkg, GitHub).
#
# Block 1, every page and file:
# - X-Frame-Options: other websites may not show this site inside a frame (clickjacking).
#   Our own YouTube player still works: that frame goes the other way.
# - Referrer-Policy: other sites see only "jcmuhire.com", never the full address.
# - Permissions-Policy: the site never uses these, so the browser refuses them outright.
#
# Block 2, built code, styles, fonts and photos: their names change whenever their content
# changes, so browsers may keep them for a year without ever showing an old version.
# Keep comment lines out of the indented blocks: there they would be read as headers.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
